''[[The Apothecary Diaries (TV series)|The Apothecary Diaries]]'' is a Japanese [[anime]] television series based on the [[light novel]] series ''[[The Apothecary Diaries]]'', written by [[Hyūganatsu (writer)|Hyūganatsu]], and illustrated by Touko Shino. Produced by [[Toho Animation Studio]] and [[OLM (studio)|OLM]], the series was written by Norihiro Naganuma and directed by Naganuma and Akinori Fudesaka. {{Ill|Yukiko Nakatani|ja|中谷友紀子}} designed the characters. The first season ran from October 22, 2023, to March 24, 2024 on [[Nippon TV]] and its affiliates.<ref name="Anime-Cast2">{{Cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|date=July 7, 2023|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-07-07/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-teaser-video-reveals-new-cast-member-october-premiere/.200074|title=The Apothecary Diaries Anime's Teaser Video Reveals New Cast Member, October Premiere|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230715121125/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-07-07/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-teaser-video-reveals-new-cast-member-october-premiere/.200074|archive-date=July 15, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=July 7, 2023}}</ref><ref name="Time" /> 

Its soundtrack was composed by [[Satoru Kōsaki]], [[Kevin Penkin]], and {{Ill|Alisa Okehazama|ja|桶狭間ありさ}}.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://mantan-web.jp/article/20230216dog00m200000000c.html|script-title=ja:薬屋のひとりごと：2023年テレビアニメ化 TOHO animation STUDIO×OLM 悠木碧が猫猫に|website=[[Mantan Web]]|language=ja|date=February 16, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230216013015/https://mantan-web.jp/article/20230216dog00m200000000c.html|archive-date=February 16, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=February 16, 2023}}</ref><ref name="Anime-Cast">{{Cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael Antonio|date=February 15, 2023|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-02-15/the-apothecary-diaries-novels-about-palace-intrigue-get-2023-tv-anime/.194948|title=The Apothecary Diaries Novels About Palace Intrigue Get 2023 TV Anime|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230216014628/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-02-15/the-apothecary-diaries-novels-about-palace-intrigue-get-2023-tv-anime/.194948|archive-date=February 16, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=February 16, 2023}}</ref> The initial opening theme song was {{Nihongo|"[[Be a Flower|Hana ni Natte]]"|花になって||{{Lit|Be a Flower}}}}, performed by [[Ryokuoushoku Shakai]]; the ending theme song was {{Nihongo|"Aikotoba"|アイコトバ||{{Lit|The Spell}}}}, performed by [[Aina the End]].<ref name="Anime-Cast3">{{Cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|date=October 1, 2023|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-10-01/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-main-promo-video-reveals-more-cast-theme-song-artists/.203024|title=The Apothecary Diaries Anime's Main Promo Video Reveals More Cast, Theme Song Artists|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231001182445/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-10-01/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-main-promo-video-reveals-more-cast-theme-song-artists/.203024|archive-date=October 1, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=October 1, 2023}}</ref> The songs were changed to the opening theme song {{Nihongo|"Ambivalent"|アンビバレント}} (performed by [[Uru (singer)|Uru]]) and the ending theme song is {{Nihongo|"Ai wa Kusuri"|愛は薬||{{Lit|Love Is Medicine}}}}, performed by {{Ill|Wacci|ja|wacci}}.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/554718|script-title=ja:「薬屋のひとりごと」第2クールに桐本拓哉＆名塚佳織 OPはUru、EDはwacciが担当|website=[[Comic Natalie]]|publisher=Natasha, Inc.|language=ja|date=December 25, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231226233303/https://natalie.mu/comic/news/554718|archive-date=December 26, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=January 7, 2024}}</ref>

After the first season was broadcast, a second season was announced. It aired from January 10 to July 4, 2025, on Nippon TV's [[Friday Anime Night]] and its affiliates.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Luster|first=Joseph|date=March 23, 2024|url=https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2024/3/23/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-announced-for-2025-premiere|title=The Apothecary Diaries Season 2 Announced for 2025 Premiere [Updated]|website=[[Crunchyroll]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20240323232944/https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/latest/2024/3/23/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-announced-for-2025-premiere|archive-date=March 23, 2024|url-status=live|access-date=March 23, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/596368|script-title=ja:「薬屋のひとりごと」第2期は来年1月から連続2クールで、ティザーPV公開|website=[[Comic Natalie]]|publisher=Natasha, Inc|language=ja|date=October 22, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241217210337/https://natalie.mu/comic/news/596368|archive-date=December 17, 2024|url-status=live|access-date=October 23, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Cayanan|first=Joanna|date=October 22, 2024|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-10-22/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-teaser-reveals-january-10-debut/.217038|title=The Apothecary Diaries Season 2's Teaser Reveals January 10 Debut|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241211192120/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-10-22/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-teaser-reveals-january-10-debut/.217038|archive-date=December 11, 2024|url-status=live|access-date=October 22, 2024}}</ref> The first opening theme song is {{Nihongo|"[[Hyakka Ryōran (song)|Hyakka Ryōran]]"|百花繚乱||{{Lit|Splendid Bounty}}}} (performed by [[Lilas Ikuta]])<ref name="S2-OP1">{{Cite web|last=Cayanan|first=Joanna|date=December 9, 2024|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-12-09/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-main-trailer-unveils-more-cast-opening-song/.218788|title=The Apothecary Diaries Season 2's Main Trailer Unveils More Cast, Opening Song|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241213011444/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-12-09/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-main-trailer-unveils-more-cast-opening-song/.218788|archive-date=December 13, 2024|url-status=live|access-date=December 9, 2024}}</ref> and the first ending theme song is {{Nihongo|"Shiawase no Recipe"|幸せのレシピ||{{Lit|The Recipe for Happiness}}}}, performed by {{Ill|Dai Hirai|ja|平井大}}.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Loo|first=Egan|date=January 4, 2025|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-01-04/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-final-trailer-unveils-dai-hirai-ending-song/.219727|title=The Apothecary Diaries Season 2's 'Final' Trailer Unveils Dai Hirai's Ending Song|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250105000809/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-01-04/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-final-trailer-unveils-dai-hirai-ending-song/.219727|archive-date=January 5, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=January 9, 2025}}</ref> The second opening theme song is {{Nihongo|"Kusushiki"|クスシキ||{{Lit|Mysterious}}}} (performed by [[Mrs. Green Apple]]) and the second ending theme song is {{Nihongo|"Hitorigoto"|ひとりごと||{{Lit|Soliloquy}}}}, performed by [[Omoinotake]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|date=March 28, 2025|title=The Apothecary Diaries Season 2 Anime Reveals Trailer, Visual, Theme Song Artists, April 4 Premiere for 2nd Part|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-03-28/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-anime-reveals-trailer-visual-theme-song-artists-april-4-premiere-/.222951|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250328225812/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-03-28/the-apothecary-diaries-season-2-anime-reveals-trailer-visual-theme-song-artists-april-4-premiere-/.222951|archive-date=March 28, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=March 28, 2025}}</ref>

After the second season was broadcast, a sequel to the series was announced.<ref>{{cite web|last=Loo|first=Egan|date=July 4, 2025|title=The Apothecary Diaries Anime Gets New Sequel|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-07-04/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-gets-new-sequel/.226308|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250704150523/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-07-04/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-gets-new-sequel/.226308|archive-date=July 4, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=July 4, 2025}}</ref> On the second anniversary of the anime's premiere, a third season was announced and is set to premiere on October 2, 2026. The season, now produced solely by OLM, will run in two parts, with its second part premiering in April 2027.<ref name="S3-Film"/><ref>{{Cite web|last=Tai|first=Anita|date=August 15, 2026|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-08-15/the-apothecary-diaries-season-3-trailer-unveils-october-2-debut-more-cast-opening-song/.240600|title=The Apothecary Diaries Season 3's Trailer Unveils October 2 Debut, More Cast, Opening Song|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260815154719/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-08-15/the-apothecary-diaries-season-3-trailer-unveils-october-2-debut-more-cast-opening-song/.240600|archive-date=August 15, 2026|url-status=live|access-date=August 15, 2026}}</ref> An animated film entitled ''The Apothecary Diaries: The Deceased Empress' Treasure'' (with a new story by Hyūganatsu) was also announced, and is scheduled to premiere in Japan on December 11, 2026. The movie will be produced solely by Toho Animation Studio.<ref name="S3-Film">{{Cite web|last=Cayanan|first=Joanna|date=October 22, 2025|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-10-22/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-confirms-season-3-original-film-in-2026/.230197|title=The Apothecary Diaries Anime Confirms Season 3, Original Film in 2026|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://archive.today/20251022093559/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-10-22/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-confirms-season-3-original-film-in-2026/.230197|archive-date=October 22, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=October 22, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|date=July 2, 2026|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-07-02/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-film-trailer-reveals-title-cast-december-11-opening/.239226|title=The Apothecary Diaries Anime Film's Trailer Reveals Title, Cast, December 11 Opening|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260702225442/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-07-02/the-apothecary-diaries-anime-film-trailer-reveals-title-cast-december-11-opening/.239226|archive-date=July 2, 2026|url-status=live|access-date=July 2, 2026}}</ref>

[[Crunchyroll]] streams the series worldwide outside Asia, including the Middle East, the [[Commonwealth of Independent States|CIS]], and South Asia.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|date=July 3, 2023|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-07-03/crunchyroll-licenses-the-apothecary-diaries-goblin-slayer-season-2-black-butler-more-anime/.199938|title=Crunchyroll Licenses The Apothecary Diaries, Goblin Slayer Season 2, Black Butler, More Anime|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230703235820/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-07-03/crunchyroll-licenses-the-apothecary-diaries-goblin-slayer-season-2-black-butler-more-anime/.199938|archive-date=July 3, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=July 3, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/seasonal-lineup/2023/9/20/fall-anime-2023-crunchyroll|title=Crunchyroll Announces Fall 2023 Anime Season Lineup! (10/1)|website=[[Crunchyroll]]|date=September 20, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231006224005/https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/seasonal-lineup/2023/9/20/fall-anime-2023-crunchyroll|archive-date=October 6, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=October 1, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Hazra|first=Adriana|date=September 22, 2023|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-09-22/crunchyroll-announces-hindi-tamil-dubs-for-jujutsu-kaisen-season-2-frieren-2-more-anime/.202697|title=Crunchyroll Announces Hindi, Tamil Dubs for Jujutsu Kaisen Season 2, Frieren, 2 More Anime|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231028181100/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2023-09-22/crunchyroll-announces-hindi-tamil-dubs-for-jujutsu-kaisen-season-2-frieren-2-more-anime/.202697|archive-date=October 28, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=October 23, 2023}}</ref> The first season's first part was released on [[Blu-ray]] on January 28, 2025, and the second part was released on March 25 of that year.<ref>{{Cite press release|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/press-release/2024-10-16/crunchyroll-to-release-the-apothecary-diaries-season-1-part-1-horimiya-the-missing-pieces-and-more-/.216790|title=Crunchyroll to Release 'The Apothecary Diaries' Season 1 Part 1, 'Horimiya: The Missing Pieces,' And More on Blu-Ray This January|website=[[Anime News Network]]|publisher=[[Crunchyroll, LLC]]|date=October 16, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241219095849/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/press-release/2024-10-16/crunchyroll-to-release-the-apothecary-diaries-season-1-part-1-horimiya-the-missing-pieces-and-more-/.216790|archive-date=December 19, 2024|url-status=live|access-date=October 23, 2024}}</ref><ref name="Part1"/><ref name="Part2"/> [[Netflix]] streams the series in some Asian regions.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Tan|first=Melvyn|date=October 1, 2023|url=https://anitrendz.net/news/2023/10/01/netflix-will-stream-the-apothecary-diaries-in-select-asian-countries/|title=Netflix Will Stream The Apothecary Diaries in "Select" Asian Countries|website=Anitrendz|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231005100832/https://anitrendz.net/news/2023/10/01/netflix-will-stream-the-apothecary-diaries-in-select-asian-countries/|archive-date=October 5, 2023|url-status=live|access-date=October 1, 2023}}</ref>

